    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point: exploiting the extremely favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez, whose 17.18 xERA presents an ideal target for **Kyle Tucker** (81.26) and **Andy Pages** (70.87). **Kyle Tucker** remains our most potent asset today, buoyed by the elite matchup and a strong lineup position that maximizes his path to R and RBI. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Josh Lowe** (71.68) also secure high-tier status, benefiting significantly from their platoon advantages against Young and Sasaki, respectively. **Sam Antonacci** (61.39) is worth monitoring; despite a neutral park environment, his elite xwOBA of 0.400 and leadoff placement provide a high floor, particularly given the league-wide premium we place on the stolen base upside he brings to the table.\n\nThe most difficult lineup decision today involved **Coby Mayo** (56.80), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Dominic Smith** (56.83). While **Coby Mayo** showcased decent power potential against Lovelady, the optimizer prioritized **Dominic Smith**\u2019s situational platoon edge, which pushed his efficiency just past the threshold required for inclusion. Risk management remains a priority: while the matchup against Rodriguez is a statistical goldmine, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.74) faces a slight regression warning due to incoming wind, and **Gunnar Henderson** (61.92) is battling a dynamic platoon disadvantage against the lefty Lovelady that suppresses his ceiling. We are holding **Jackson Merrill** (51.78) and **Miguel Vargas** (52.02) in reserve; while their skill profiles are solid, the pitching matchups against Kirby and Rea respectively made them the odd men out in a competitive starting field.",
